-- title:
--   Descended fixed field of the rigid level model equals F₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$, an inclusion $hle$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(M')$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$, where $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, a constant reduction $R_0$ along $A$, a point $s\in W$, a subfield $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with elements $\pi_0,\zeta_0,\varpi_t,\xi\in k_0$ and $\pi_0\in A$, a natural number $\ell$, a subfield $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ induced by $A$ and $\varpi_b\in A_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ carrying an algebra structure over $A\cap k_0$ compatible with $k_0$, a nonzero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t'$ and $a_0$ of $A\cap k_0$, an ideal $y$ of the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ of $(A\cap k_0, K_\ell, j_\ell)$, a subalgebra $B_t$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$, natural numbers $n,m$, $\gamma_0\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal, the hypothesis that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$ lies in $K_\ell$, a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and a term $\mathcal F$ of `RigidDescentHyps` for all these data, which records the rigid-descent hypotheses (among them $q\ge 5$, $q\nmid M'$, $\ell'\ge 3$, $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, that $\xi$ is a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity and that $K_\ell$ is the coefficientwise base change to $k_0$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$). Let $G$ be the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, i.e. $\tau$ transforms ratios of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_H$ according to the slash action of $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ under every complex embedding sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$; let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ be the subalgebra of $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ whose members are exactly the elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in (the image of) $k_0$, there is a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi : K_0 \to F_0$ such that: (1) for every $f\in K_0$ the coefficientwise image of $f$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\ell'$ applied to $\varphi(f)$, i.e. the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{\ell'}$; (2) for every $\zeta$ in $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity $\xi'\in k_0$ with $\zeta = (\xi')^{\ell'}$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi'\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma\,K_\ell\,\tau$, the field $K_0$ is $\tau$-stable and $\varphi\circ\tau = \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\circ\varphi$ on $K_0$; (3) for every $g$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ such that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g)$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends that element to the image under $hle$ of the coefficientwise base change $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,g$.
--
--   This identifies the $G$-fixed subfield $K_0$ of the rigid auxiliary-level field $K_\ell$ with the level-$q^2M'$ field $F_0$ over $k_0$, compatibly with undoing the $\ell'$-expansion, with the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ attached to pairs $(\zeta,\gamma)$, and with the rational modular functions of level $M'$. It is the descent step of the rigid-level construction, used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart).
